<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1276"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, October 24, 2004 - 9:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->See his post in Messages From BTK section. <BR> <BR>Quote: <BR>__________________________________________ <BR>Posted on Monday, Oct 11, 2004 - 11:15 am:      <BR> <BR>her shoes were together sir <BR>__________________________________________ <BR> <BR>I say Kent is a phony. His sentence neither starts with a capital letter nor ends with punctuation. Ok, the teacher in me just had to point that out. lol <BR> <BR>Everyone knows BTK is a very wordy guy. His first letter, inside the engineering book, was two pages of typed information that was single spaced.   <BR> <BR>Hey, Kent. Why don&#39;t you answer Tom&#39;s message to you? <BR>-Deb<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1276-->
<!--Post: 1343--><!--Time: 1099452239-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1343"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ksguy2178<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ksguy2178<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, November 02, 2004 - 7:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Wasn&#39;t this posting related to the interview with the retired employee of the Wichita Police Department when he discussed BTK drawing pictures from memory and drew Nancy Fox&#39;s shoes together instead of apart?  The link I am referring to is at: <a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/inside.html" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/inside.html</a>.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1343-->
<!--Post: 1344--><!--Time: 1099496453-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1344"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, November 03, 2004 - 7:40 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->KsGuy, thanks for the link. Kent is not BTK. He is only posting and showing off. If he was BTK, he would have responded to Tom by now. <BR> <BR>If the real BTK drew the sketch of Nancy Fox&#39;s shoes together, it is probably because he placed them that way himself and someone at the crime scene picked them up to examine them and did not set them straight again. Also her sweater was draped on the chair. When she came home tired from work, did she throw it on the couch or bed? He may have dramatically draped her sweater on the chair because he is obsessed with neatness. Perhaps the only reason he left the contents of the victims&#39; purses dumped out is because he wanted WPD to know he had done it.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1344-->
<!--Post: 1349--><!--Time: 1099510320-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1349"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Interested<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Interested<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, November 03, 2004 - 11:32 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think that btk is someone that frew up in the area and had a really bad childhood.I think he is not killing people at random but in fact is killing people that he knew as a child.This might explian the reasoning for the baby picture.I do not think that kent is btk......but then again who knows.With all the attention this guys likes you would think he would post better messages.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1349-->
<!--Post: 1351--><!--Time: 1099519281-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1351"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, November 03, 2004 - 2:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Interested, your message is much appreciated. BTK may have had a good childhood, with a nice family. They may have been poor or middle class, but they were a hardworking and loving family. Yet the parents’ religious upbringing, “spare the rod and spoil the child,” probably meant that he was often punished. He might have older brothers and sisters who were “good” and got all the attention. The family felt like he did not measure up to their high standards. Since he could never be as “good” as the family wanted him to be, he became sullen and depressed. Each time his siblings got attention and praise for their goodness and he got punished for his wrongdoings, he began to get angry and have evil thoughts. The only fun he experienced was when reading or watching TV. &#40;There were no videos or computer back in the days of his childhood.&#41; In order to escape from his lonely and wretched existence, he secluded himself from the family and began reading books, newspapers, and magazines. If only he had read more of the classical literature and not crime and serial killer stuff, maybe he would not have gone down the wrong road. &#40;Maybe his use of videos and computers is what kept him busy all these years before he resurfaced.&#41; Of course this is pure speculation and very simplistic at that. BTK will probably reveal that he was abused as a child and that is the reason that he got off the right track and headed down a one way street to a dead end.  <BR>-Deb <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1351-->
<!--Post: 1539--><!--Time: 1101969440-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1539"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Das<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Das<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 01, 2004 - 10:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Someone has probably already pointed this out.  I hate to say what seems obvious, but the first initials of kent t billingham backwards are btk.  I thought that was interesting if he is btk and he apparently chose a rather cryptic thing to write.  I wouldn&#39;t rule him out too quickly.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
